Common Mortgage Mistakes to Avoid

Just as important as knowing what to do is understanding what not to do. Some of the most common mistakes homebuyers make include:
    • Only checking rates with one lender. Rates and fees can vary meaningfully between lenders, so comparing options is worth the extra time. 
    • Making large purchases before closing. Financing a car or opening new credit accounts before closing can affect your debt-to-income ratio and jeopardize your approved rate. 
    • Ignoring the full cost of homeownership. Property taxes, insurance, and HOA fees (where applicable) all factor into what you can realistically afford. 
    • Waiting too long to get pre-approved. In a competitive housing market, being pre-approved early can strengthen your offer and give you more negotiating power. 

